  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening of fiscal control through improved citizen participation and SAI&apos;s institutional capacities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant would continue the Bank&apos;s support to the Central American Organization of Supreme Audit Institutions (OCCEFS), building up on its successful ongoing partnership, while recognizing the inherent long term/continuous improvement nature of public financial accountability reforms. The grant would have two development objectives: (i) to strengthen the capacity of OCCEFS members to construct more effective partnerships with civil society organizations on financial accountability matters; and (ii) to strengthen the capacity of OCCEFS members to develop auditor certifications, prepare sectoral studies, and improve the impact of their work with the legislative branch. These objectives would be met by taking advantage of economies of scale in the regional production of adaptable common tools. The grant development objective is to strengthen the capacity of OCCEFS (Organizaci&#xf3;n Centroamericana y del Caribe de Entidades Fiscalizadoras Superiores) members to construct more effective partnerships with civil society organizations on financial accountability matters. The objective would be met by taking advantage of economies of scale in the regional production of adaptable common tools.</narrative>
  </description>
